1
00:00:00,790 --> 00:00:01,990
Miyata?

2
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:07,770
What about the payment...?

3
00:00:08,670 --> 00:00:10,860
I paid it all in full.

4
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,780
So...

5
00:00:17,510 --> 00:00:18,660
don't worry.

6
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:19,930
But...

7
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:21,770
Hm?

8
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:25,140
I want to pay for half of it too.

9
00:00:25,730 --> 00:00:29,360
How about this?
You pay me a set amount each month.

10
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:31,360
I'll register the place
under both of our names.

11
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:33,240
If you do that...

12
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:35,220
won't that trigger gift taxes?

13
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:36,700
Look at that.

14
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:39,660
You're always so sharp
about things like that.

15
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:42,220
Please don't change the subject.

16
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:43,660
Sorry.

17
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,850
Why buy this place to begin with...?

18
00:00:51,090 --> 00:00:52,420
I just thought...

19
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,130
that through this contract,

20
00:00:55,050 --> 00:00:57,740
I could make my feelings for you tangible.

21
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:00,260
Still...

22
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:03,920
what if your feelings change someday?

23
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:05,890
They won't.

24
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:10,750
What if you regret
paying for the whole thing?

25
00:01:12,390 --> 00:01:14,280
Never.

26
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:18,870
So...

27
00:01:19,910 --> 00:01:21,640
I need you to trust me.

28
00:01:26,870 --> 00:01:28,160
I really...

29
00:01:28,420 --> 00:01:30,350
can't move in.

30
00:01:31,590 --> 00:01:33,810
Not until I can pay my fair share.

31
00:01:37,090 --> 00:01:40,140
I guess I was rushing things.

32
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:59,800
"Love is Better the Second Time Around season2"
(Episode 5)

33
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:24,430
Even though I said that...

34
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:27,180
making as much money as he does...

35
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:29,410
who knows how long that will take?

36
00:02:32,230 --> 00:02:33,020
Editor-in-Chief.

37
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:33,850
Yeah?

38
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:36,950
I shared the draft cover design
for Teacher Iwanaga's book.

39
00:02:37,150 --> 00:02:38,310
All right, let's have a look.

40
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:42,000
Hey, this looks pretty good!

41
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:44,260
It might even be a bestseller!

42
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:47,079
You better give me a hefty bonus if it is.

43
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,080
Sure, sure.

44
00:02:48,910 --> 00:02:49,920
All right.

45
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:51,920
Could I have everyone's
attention for a moment?

46
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:54,920
As most of you probably already know,

47
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:58,799
we brought in consultants six months ago...

48
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,700
to spearhead corporate reforms.

49
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:06,370
Now, BusinessNow will also
be working under their guidance.

50
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:07,840
So, I'd like to introduce her.

51
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:09,340
Masumoto-san, please.

52
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:15,020
I'm Masumoto Yuko from Veritas Partners.

53
00:03:15,070 --> 00:03:16,956
Starting tomorrow, I'll be
working alongside you all.

54
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:18,490
I look forward to working with you.

55
00:03:20,030 --> 00:03:21,030
Welcome aboard.

56
00:03:34,210 --> 00:03:36,240
No matter how bad things get at work...

57
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:39,080
he's always waiting for me at home.

58
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:43,680
Welcome home.

59
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:49,700
I always thought you were
just naturally good-looking.

60
00:03:49,810 --> 00:03:51,970
I didn't realize you worked
so hard behind the scenes.

61
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:55,620
Want to join me, Miyata?

62
00:03:56,110 --> 00:03:58,510
You're reaching the age where
you need to maintain yourself.

63
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:00,990
I don't gain weight easily.

64
00:04:01,530 --> 00:04:02,530
That's exactly what...

65
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:04,990
I used to say a year ago.

66
00:04:05,450 --> 00:04:08,840
Middle age sneaks up
on you before you know it.

67
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:11,970
I'm two years younger
than you. I'll be fine.

68
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:20,049
What's going on?

69
00:04:20,050 --> 00:04:22,900
Why make something so
elaborate out of nowhere?

70
00:04:23,130 --> 00:04:25,860
I just wanted to make you happy.

71
00:04:31,850 --> 00:04:33,810
Organic tomatoes...

72
00:04:34,390 --> 00:04:35,660
and Yonezawa beef.

73
00:04:37,190 --> 00:04:39,790
You went to that upscale
supermarket again, didn't you?

74
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:42,670
Is that a bad thing?

75
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,990
The cheap stuff is fine.

76
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:48,600
Cheap ingredients work just as well.

77
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:51,720
We need to save for retirement.

78
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:55,790
All right.

79
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:59,340
What are we making today?

80
00:04:59,630 --> 00:05:00,630
Today...

81
00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:03,479
we're making your favorite: Caprese salad.

82
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,480
Oh!

83
00:05:06,970 --> 00:05:08,550
Like this?

84
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:10,660
A little more... Slice it like this.

85
00:05:10,890 --> 00:05:11,890
Just slice it gently.

86
00:05:13,390 --> 00:05:14,390
Yeah, exactly.

87
00:05:18,110 --> 00:05:19,150
Do you know how to cut it?

88
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:22,880
Hey, wait, I'm holding a knife!
Watch out, that's dangerous!

89
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:24,360
Why don't you cut it then?

90
00:05:24,361 --> 00:05:25,780
All right, I'll do it.

91
00:05:30,450 --> 00:05:31,680
How was your day?

92
00:05:32,950 --> 00:05:34,180
You mean at work?

93
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:35,580
Yeah.

94
00:05:37,750 --> 00:05:40,060
Nothing special. The usual.

95
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:45,190
You look like you have a lot on your mind.

96
00:05:48,590 --> 00:05:50,430
Maybe the ingredients
are just too high-end.

97
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:53,120
My stomach's in shock.

98
00:05:57,480 --> 00:06:01,080
These are the latest sales
numbers for BusinessNow.

99
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:04,750
Both our magazines and
books are trending downward.

100
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,990
As you know,

101
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:10,990
the entire publishing
industry is struggling right now.

102
00:06:11,410 --> 00:06:14,280
Fretting over the status
quo won't solve anything.

103
00:06:16,540 --> 00:06:19,410
The real question is how
we adapt and fight back.

104
00:06:19,630 --> 00:06:22,450
I want us to figure that out together.

105
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:25,860
Miyata-san.

106
00:06:26,590 --> 00:06:27,590
Yes?

107
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:29,560
What project are you currently working on?

108
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:31,720
Well...

109
00:06:31,930 --> 00:06:35,090
I'm collaborating with Associate Professor
Iwanaga Takashi of Tooh University...

110
00:06:35,220 --> 00:06:38,990
on a book exploring
emerging business models.

111
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:40,790
And the promotional plan?

112
00:06:42,020 --> 00:06:43,690
Aside from securing promotional blurbs...

113
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:46,740
from several prominent academics,

114
00:06:47,030 --> 00:06:49,399
we're aiming for at least
two newspaper reviews...

115
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:50,400
Stop.

116
00:06:52,070 --> 00:06:56,300
Young people read less
and less text these days.

117
00:06:56,950 --> 00:06:57,930
So,

118
00:06:57,960 --> 00:07:01,040
where do they get their information?

119
00:07:03,130 --> 00:07:04,340
From videos?

120
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:06,000
Precisely.

121
00:07:07,630 --> 00:07:10,670
Submit a video promotion
proposal by tomorrow.

122
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:12,430
By tomorrow?!

123
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:15,810
Here.

124
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:16,810
Thank you.

125
00:07:16,890 --> 00:07:19,359
I'll file this on the
document shelf right away.

126
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:20,690
Thanks, appreciate it.

127
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,660
Shiraishi.

128
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:26,640
Is there a budget supermarket around here?

129
00:07:27,730 --> 00:07:29,250
Budget?!

130
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:30,320
Yeah.

131
00:07:30,530 --> 00:07:33,860
Bargains, discount
specials, that sort of thing.

132
00:07:35,530 --> 00:07:36,990
Why the sudden interest?

133
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:41,960
Miyata chewed me out for
always buying pricey groceries.

134
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:47,840
That...

135
00:07:48,130 --> 00:07:49,760
That little jerk...

136
00:07:50,380 --> 00:07:51,380
Hm?

137
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:57,390
That would be Asahi supermarket.

138
00:07:57,560 --> 00:08:00,020
Just walk straight out the main entrance.

139
00:08:01,190 --> 00:08:02,190
Thanks.

140
00:08:02,390 --> 00:08:03,520
That really helps.

141
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:07,610
Asahi supermarket, huh...?

142
00:08:17,030 --> 00:08:18,160
I'm home.

143
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:19,700
Welcome back.

144
00:08:21,830 --> 00:08:24,420
I bought budget ingredients today.

145
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:26,540
Pea sprouts,

146
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:29,340
bean sprouts,

147
00:08:31,050 --> 00:08:32,860
and chicken on sale.

148
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,610
I have to finish a proposal by tomorrow.

149
00:08:41,230 --> 00:08:42,230
Oh...

150
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:44,980
I see.

151
00:08:48,070 --> 00:08:49,070
Well then,

152
00:08:49,730 --> 00:08:53,050
I'll put your plate in the
fridge. Be sure to eat later.

153
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:55,360
I'm sorry.

154
00:09:12,090 --> 00:09:13,860
Come sit here for a second.

155
00:09:31,570 --> 00:09:32,750
Why are you...

156
00:09:33,570 --> 00:09:36,130
so good to me?

157
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:39,240
Because you've been so swamped lately.

158
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:44,180
Do I look that overwhelmed?

159
00:09:44,370 --> 00:09:45,580
It definitely shows.

160
00:09:50,710 --> 00:09:51,710
Does that hit the spot?

161
00:09:52,210 --> 00:09:53,730
That feels amazing...

162
00:09:55,920 --> 00:09:59,190
I wish I could ease what's
troubling your mind just as easily.

163
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:07,410
You can lean on me, you know.

164
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:22,660
Actually...

165
00:10:22,870 --> 00:10:25,350
a consultant was assigned
to our department.

166
00:10:25,370 --> 00:10:26,620
Is that so?

167
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:32,420
She out of nowhere ordered
me to make a promo video.

168
00:10:32,590 --> 00:10:33,590
A video?

169
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:37,270
Like interviewing you on camera.

170
00:10:38,130 --> 00:10:39,690
I'd gladly do it.

171
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:44,040
I really appreciate that,

172
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:46,910
but I don't want to appear on screen.

173
00:10:49,350 --> 00:10:51,730
I'm terrible in front of
people to begin with.

174
00:10:52,230 --> 00:10:54,550
Let alone in a video that'll
stay on the internet forever.

175
00:10:54,610 --> 00:10:56,010
I just can't bring myself to do it.

176
00:10:58,150 --> 00:10:59,320
I see...

177
00:11:01,450 --> 00:11:02,450
In that case...

178
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:06,540
Huh?

179
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:22,090
Hotta-san, I had no idea you
had such a professional camera.

180
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:24,930
I used to work in video production.

181
00:11:24,970 --> 00:11:26,599
Did some part-time
gigs at a TV station too.

182
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:27,600
Wow...

183
00:11:33,810 --> 00:11:35,860
Camera crew is ready!

184
00:11:37,150 --> 00:11:38,150
All right.

185
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:51,890
Am I in the shot?

186
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:53,930
We'll edit you out later, so don't worry.

187
00:11:55,290 --> 00:11:56,290
Okay.

188
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:58,050
Rolling!

189
00:11:58,670 --> 00:12:00,300
Three, two...

190
00:12:05,180 --> 00:12:06,180
Hello, everyone!

191
00:12:06,710 --> 00:12:09,030
My name is Business Bear!

192
00:12:09,730 --> 00:12:12,640
Today on Business Bear's Classroom,

193
00:12:12,810 --> 00:12:15,660
we're introducing this
brand-new book fresh off the press:

194
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:19,290
"Finding Tomorrow's Value"!

195
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:22,150
And the author behind it,

196
00:12:23,370 --> 00:12:27,300
with a smile as sweet
as strawberry shortcake??

197
00:12:27,740 --> 00:12:29,620
Tooh University Associate Professor...

198
00:12:29,830 --> 00:12:31,500
Teacher Iwanaga Takashi!

199
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:33,080
I'm Iwanaga.

200
00:12:33,460 --> 00:12:34,710
Pleasure to be here.

201
00:12:35,580 --> 00:12:36,840
Teacher, Teacher!

202
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:38,340
Will this book...

203
00:12:38,590 --> 00:12:41,340
be too difficult for me to understand?

204
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:42,380
Not at all.

205
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:44,720
It's written in clear, simple terms,

206
00:12:44,970 --> 00:12:47,550
so even Business Bear can enjoy reading it.

207
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:58,480
Miyata-san, Business Bear is so adorable!

208
00:12:58,610 --> 00:13:00,280
Oh, thank you.

209
00:13:06,990 --> 00:13:08,160
Very cute.

210
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:11,120
Thanks.

211
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:19,310
You've been wearing
that watch a lot lately.

212
00:13:20,210 --> 00:13:21,880
My other one broke.

213
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:24,380
Oh...

214
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:31,720
Three, two...

215
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:35,140
Action!

216
00:13:35,270 --> 00:13:36,600
Teacher, I have a question!

217
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:37,770
What is it?

218
00:13:38,190 --> 00:13:41,280
What does "re-entering a market" mean?

219
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:46,490
It refers to a company returning to a
market it previously walked away from.

220
00:13:47,070 --> 00:13:49,200
Why would they go back?

221
00:13:49,550 --> 00:13:50,550
Well...

222
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:54,960
Market conditions might have shifted,
or competitors might have gone under.

223
00:13:55,250 --> 00:13:56,850
There are many different reasons.

224
00:13:59,330 --> 00:14:00,580
Let's start over.

225
00:14:01,420 --> 00:14:04,860
Neither of us has to worry about
climbing the corporate ladder anymore.

226
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:07,220
We can finally face each other honestly.

227
00:14:09,390 --> 00:14:10,930
- Is this spot okay?
- Yes.

228
00:14:16,060 --> 00:14:17,060
However,

229
00:14:17,140 --> 00:14:18,730
doing so is also very costly.

230
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:21,870
Reclaiming what was once lost...

231
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:24,320
isn't easy, is it?

232
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:25,530
Right.

233
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:28,210
If the returning party is formidable,

234
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:32,430
and the incumbents haven't
built a solid enough foundation,

235
00:14:32,620 --> 00:14:34,700
they could end up completely swept away.

236
00:14:44,630 --> 00:14:46,470
That might have been a little too profound.

237
00:14:48,260 --> 00:14:49,610
Let's do another take.

238
00:14:50,510 --> 00:14:51,510
Okay.

239
00:14:57,230 --> 00:14:58,830
I'm so glad the shoot went smoothly.

240
00:14:59,980 --> 00:15:01,830
All thanks to Teacher Iwanaga.

241
00:15:13,010 --> 00:15:15,580
Cleaning up might take a bit,
so feel free to head out first.

242
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:17,200
All right.

243
00:15:17,910 --> 00:15:20,590
I actually need to pick up a few
things before heading home anyway.

244
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:23,250
There's something I'm looking for.

245
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:26,880
I see.

246
00:15:27,550 --> 00:15:28,920
See you later, then.

247
00:15:32,510 --> 00:15:33,510
Yeah.

248
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:39,559
I'll be taking off now.

249
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:41,060
Thank you so much.

250
00:16:41,370 --> 00:16:42,460
A video?

251
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:48,210
Hasegawa-san's approach has
changed quite a bit since I left.

252
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:52,510
The Editor-in-Chief didn't really have
a choice with the consultant pushing...

253
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:54,720
Consultants, huh?

254
00:16:55,590 --> 00:16:59,520
Ever since I went freelance, at least
nobody is breathing down my neck anymore.

255
00:16:59,850 --> 00:17:02,350
It's tough work, but the
freedom makes it worth it.

256
00:17:03,020 --> 00:17:06,690
You've always done better
without constraints, Seki-san.

257
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:08,440
Unlike me.

258
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:10,420
Who knows?

259
00:17:13,030 --> 00:17:15,280
Actually, I got married recently.

260
00:17:16,070 --> 00:17:17,070
Wait, really?

261
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:19,240
Congratulations!

262
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:22,660
I thought about going
back to corporate life,

263
00:17:22,870 --> 00:17:24,080
but in the end,

264
00:17:24,370 --> 00:17:26,250
I figured I'd see how
far I can take this path.

265
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:29,340
What about you, Miyata?

266
00:17:30,670 --> 00:17:31,670
About what?

267
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:35,430
Are you seeing someone?
Thinking about marriage?

268
00:17:37,930 --> 00:17:39,326
Or should I not pry into
personal stuff like that these days?

269
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:40,350
Well...

270
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:45,080
We're not coworkers anymore anyway.

271
00:17:45,230 --> 00:17:46,230
Here.

272
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:49,190
Well...

273
00:17:51,230 --> 00:17:52,230
I do have someone.

274
00:17:53,490 --> 00:17:54,880
We're living together right now.

275
00:17:57,590 --> 00:17:58,590
Then...

276
00:17:58,910 --> 00:18:00,010
it's only a matter of time?

277
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:04,660
Maybe...

278
00:18:05,730 --> 00:18:06,730
Yeah.

279
00:18:09,250 --> 00:18:10,250
Anyway,

280
00:18:10,510 --> 00:18:11,510
let's both

281
00:18:12,090 --> 00:18:15,050
work hard so our happiness lasts for good.

282
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:17,260
Sure.

283
00:18:18,930 --> 00:18:20,760
Cheers.

284
00:18:46,290 --> 00:18:50,000
Can we really... make our happiness last?

285
00:19:33,250 --> 00:19:35,460
"My name is Business Bear!"

286
00:19:36,270 --> 00:19:42,220
This segment features Business Bear
introducing our company's publications.

287
00:19:42,590 --> 00:19:45,760
Moving forward, we plan to bring
in higher-grade filming equipment,

288
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:49,890
and produce an original plush
mascot specifically for shooting.

289
00:19:50,140 --> 00:19:53,060
While Teacher Iwanaga's
charisma was certainly a factor,

290
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:54,650
Miyata-san,

291
00:19:54,980 --> 00:19:57,110
I had no idea you were so gifted at this.

292
00:19:58,110 --> 00:19:59,280
Thank you, but...

293
00:20:00,820 --> 00:20:05,200
We want to develop Business
Bear into one of our flagship IPs.

294
00:20:05,740 --> 00:20:08,040
I see. Turning it into an IP.

295
00:20:09,370 --> 00:20:11,790
Then why not apply that to the book itself?

296
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:13,880
Excuse me?

297
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:16,750
Let's restructure Teacher Iwanaga's book...

298
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:20,090
and release it as volume one of
the "Business Bear's Classroom" series.

299
00:20:20,670 --> 00:20:22,630
Wait a moment.

300
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:24,640
You can't just make
an arbitrary call like that.

301
00:20:25,300 --> 00:20:31,140
Director Tanabe has given me full authority
over all decisions regarding this department.

302
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:37,070
Still...

303
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:40,650
We've poured six months into this book,

304
00:20:41,900 --> 00:20:44,950
and we've built a relationship
of trust with Teacher Iwanaga...

305
00:20:45,410 --> 00:20:48,800
I'll explain everything
to him properly myself.

306
00:20:55,460 --> 00:20:56,500
Hasegawa-san.

307
00:20:56,750 --> 00:20:57,750
Yeah?

308
00:20:58,550 --> 00:21:01,050
Is that set in stone?

309
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:02,510
No.

310
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:05,150
I'll push back and talk
to upper management.

311
00:21:05,970 --> 00:21:07,260
Thank you...

312
00:21:08,010 --> 00:21:09,260
Though...

313
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:12,520
honestly, I think the chances are slim.

314
00:21:13,770 --> 00:21:14,770
What?

315
00:21:16,610 --> 00:21:21,360
Maybe this company doesn't
need people like us anymore.

316
00:21:25,740 --> 00:21:27,900
Might be time to think about
branching out on our own.

317
00:22:04,110 --> 00:22:05,210
You're home.

318
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:12,660
Um...

319
00:22:13,620 --> 00:22:16,700
Before buying an apartment, there was
something else I should have done first.

320
00:22:18,210 --> 00:22:19,730
No matter what, this one thing...

321
00:22:20,250 --> 00:22:21,980
I had to be the one to do it.

322
00:22:24,340 --> 00:22:25,550
This one thing?

323
00:22:26,550 --> 00:22:27,970
I once told you, didn't I?

324
00:22:29,220 --> 00:22:31,410
That the weight of love is invisible.

325
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:33,180
Do you remember?

326
00:22:35,770 --> 00:22:38,000
I think... you did.

327
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:41,710
I take that back.

328
00:22:44,610 --> 00:22:46,090
I want you to feel it.

329
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:48,630
The weight of this love...

330
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:56,620
right on your ring finger.

331
00:23:09,640 --> 00:23:11,140
Miyata Akihiro...

332
00:23:12,640 --> 00:23:15,520
Will you be my partner for life?

333
00:23:30,990 --> 00:23:32,420
I'm sorry!

334
00:23:45,460 --> 00:23:48,509
[Next Episode]
Have we both just grown up too much?

335
00:23:48,510 --> 00:23:49,470
Long time no see.

336
00:23:49,471 --> 00:23:50,909
Did you two date before?

337
00:23:50,910 --> 00:23:53,010
There can be second chances, right?

338
00:23:53,390 --> 00:23:54,679
Just like us.

339
00:23:54,680 --> 00:23:56,490
When I love you this much...

340
00:23:56,520 --> 00:23:59,690
Please just forget about me.
